{
  "$comment": [
    "Documentation coverage manifest — the currency contract for this repo's markdown.",
    "",
    "PURPOSE. A document is OUT OF DATE when the thing it describes has changed since",
    "the document was last verified against it. Age alone is not the signal: a stable",
    "spec can be old and correct, a recently-touched doc can be wrong. This manifest",
    "supplies the two facts that make staleness computable — what each document covers,",
    "and when it was last verified.",
    "",
    "EXHAUSTIVE. Every tracked *.md must appear here exactly once. A file that is not",
    "listed is itself a finding: `npm run docs-check` reports it as UNCLASSIFIED. That",
    "rule is the whole point — without it this manifest reproduces, one level up, the",
    "bug it exists to prevent (the document nobody thought of).",
    "",
    "CLASSES.",
    "  shipped    Copied into every release package. Users read these. Stale -> ALWAYS",
    "             auto-added to the sprint plan.",
    "  governed   Internal docs describing compiler behavior. Stale -> the N most-stale",
    "             are auto-added per sprint (see policy.autoAddGovernedPerSprint).",
    "  process    Docs about how we work. Not staled by source changes; reviewed when",
    "             the process itself changes.",
    "  historical A record of what was true when written. Never stale by definition.",
    "             Rewriting history is not a documentation update.",
    "  generated  Produced by tooling. Regenerate, do not hand-edit.",
    "",
    "VERIFIED. For shipped/governed entries, `verified` is the release version the doc",
    "was last checked against. A doc is stale when any file matching its covered areas",
    "has a commit newer than the tag for `verified`. Set it only after actually",
    "re-reading the document against the code — it is a claim, not a timestamp.",
    "  null = never verified under this scheme; treated as stale on first run.",
    "",
    "  A PARTIAL UPDATE DOES NOT EARN THE STAMP. `verified` means the WHOLE document",
    "  was checked, not the section you happened to change. Editing one section and",
    "  stamping the file marks the untouched sections as current when nobody looked at",
    "  them — which is worse than leaving it stale, because stale is visible in the",
    "  report and a false stamp is not.",
    "",
    "  Learned the hard way, 2026-08-08: Preprocessor.md was stamped 1.55.2 after its",
    "  Diagnostics, #error, #warn and #undef sections were rewritten and verified",
    "  against the binary. Its Predefined Symbols table was never read, and carried",
    "  three errors — a symbol name that does not exist (__PNUTTS__ vs the actual",
    "  __PNUT_TS__), a wrong value for __propeller__, and __VERSION__ documented as",
    "  usable when it is defined too late for the preprocessor to ever see it.",
    "",
    "  If you can only verify part of a document, leave `verified` where it was and",
    "  note what still needs reading. Half a verification is not a verification."
  ],

  "policy": {
    "autoAddGovernedPerSprint": 3,
    "shippedAlwaysAutoAdd": true,
    "note": "Auto-added means the document becomes a numbered plan section. Removing one requires a stated reason recorded in the plan. See .claude/skills/sprint-plan/project-overlay.md"
  },

